IMPORT `sga3-76b`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: ss 76C, 76D, 76DA and 76E -- the authority for a purchase or acquisition by a company of its own shares.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Lines 8509-8935 of inputs/CoA1967.txt (a rendering, not the official text).
--
-- s 76C an off-market purchase on an equal access scheme (general meeting); s 76D a selective off-market purchase (special resolution, with no
-- votes from the sellers or their associated persons); s 76DA a contingent purchase contract (special resolution); s 76E a market purchase
-- (general meeting). The notice contents, the inspection of the agreement, the variation and release of an agreement, the class consents
-- added by Act 24 of 2025 (wef 06/05/2026) and the way the maximum price may be fixed are encoded subsection by subsection.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- Tags {F-..} point at the fork register and {MR-a}, {MR-b} at the marginal readings for a lawyer (NOTES.md).

§ `Section 76C: authority for off-market acquisition on an equal access scheme`

-- "otherwise than on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore (called in this section an off-market purchase)".
-- The first input is the fact the keel's "approved exchange in Singapore" asks (s 4(1), the Securities and Futures Act 2001 is not a source).
-- src:8511 | 76C.—(1) A company, whether or not it is listed on an approved
-- src:8512 | exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore,
-- src:8513 | may make a purchase or acquisition of its own shares otherwise than
-- src:8514 | on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange
-- src:8515 | outside Singapore (called in this section an off‑market purchase) if
-- src:8516 | the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with an equal
-- src:8517 | access scheme authorised in advance by the company in general
-- src:8518 | meeting.
@ref s 76C(1) (src:8511-8518)
GIVEN `the exchange on which the purchase or acquisition is made is an approved exchange as defined in section 2(1) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase or acquisition is made on a securities exchange outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76C(1) the purchase or acquisition is an off-market purchase` MEANS
    IF    (`s 4(1) "approved exchange in Singapore" the exchange is an approved exchange in Singapore` `the exchange on which the purchase or acquisition is made is an approved exchange as defined in section 2(1) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
      AND (NOT `the purchase or acquisition is made on a securities exchange outside Singapore`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "otherwise than on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore (called in this section an off-market purchase)" (a definition) {MR-a}

-- src:8511 | 76C.—(1) A company, whether or not it is listed on an approved
-- src:8512 | exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore,
-- src:8513 | may make a purchase or acquisition of its own shares otherwise than
-- src:8514 | on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange
-- src:8515 | outside Singapore (called in this section an off‑market purchase) if
-- src:8516 | the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with an equal
-- src:8517 | access scheme authorised in advance by the company in general
-- src:8518 | meeting.
@ref s 76C(1) (src:8511-8518)
GIVEN `the purchase or acquisition is an off-market purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with an equal access scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equal access scheme was authorised in advance by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76C(1) the company may make an off-market purchase or acquisition of its own shares` MEANS
    IF    `the purchase or acquisition is an off-market purchase`
      AND `the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with an equal access scheme`
      AND `the equal access scheme was authorised in advance by the company in general meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("A company, whether or not it is listed ..., may make a purchase or acquisition of its own shares ... if the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with an equal access scheme authorised in advance by the company in general meeting") whose "if" gate failed; the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1 {F-C1} {MR-b}

-- (2)(c) and its twins in 76D(3)(a) and 76E(2)(c): the expiry date "must not be later than the date on which the next annual general meeting of the company is or is required by law to be held, whichever is the earlier".
-- src:8532 | (c) specify a date on which the authority is to expire, being a
-- src:8533 | date that must not be later than the date on which the next
-- src:8534 | annual general meeting of the company is or is required by
-- src:8535 | law to be held, whichever is the earlier; and
@ref s 76C(2)(c) (src:8532-8535)
GIVEN `the date specified in the notice on which the authority is to expire` IS A DATE
      `the date the next annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE
      `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 76C(2)(c) the expiry date is not later than the date of the next annual general meeting` MEANS
    `the date specified in the notice on which the authority is to expire` AT MOST `s 76B(4)(b) the date the relevant period expires` `the date the next annual general meeting is held` `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held`

-- src:8522 | (2) The notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution to
-- src:8523 | authorise an off‑market purchase must —
-- src:8525 | (a) specify the maximum number of shares or the maximum
-- src:8526 | percentage of ordinary shares authorised to be purchased
-- src:8527 | or acquired;
-- src:8529 | (b) determine the maximum price which may be paid for the
-- src:8530 | shares;
-- src:8532 | (c) specify a date on which the authority is to expire, being a
-- src:8533 | date that must not be later than the date on which the next
-- src:8534 | annual general meeting of the company is or is required by
-- src:8535 | law to be held, whichever is the earlier; and
-- src:8537 | (d) specify the sources of funds to be used for the purchase or
-- src:8538 | acquisition including the amount of financing and its
-- src:8539 | impact on the company’s financial position.
@ref s 76C(2) (src:8522-8539)
GIVEN `the notice specifies the maximum number of shares or the maximum percentage of ordinary shares authorised to be purchased or acquired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice determines the maximum price which may be paid for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date specified in the notice on which the authority is to expire` IS A DATE
      `the date the next annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE
      `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held` IS A DATE
      `the notice specifies the sources of funds to be used for the purchase or acquisition including the amount of financing and its impact on the company's financial position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76C(2) the notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution has the content the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the notice specifies the maximum number of shares or the maximum percentage of ordinary shares authorised to be purchased or acquired`
      AND `the notice determines the maximum price which may be paid for the shares`
      AND `s 76C(2)(c) the expiry date is not later than the date of the next annual general meeting` `the date specified in the notice on which the authority is to expire` `the date the next annual general meeting is held` `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held`
      AND `the notice specifies the sources of funds to be used for the purchase or acquisition including the amount of financing and its impact on the company's financial position`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution to authorise an off-market purchase must — (a) specify ...; (b) determine ...; (c) specify a date ...; and (d) specify ..." (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-C2} {MR-a}

-- src:8546 | (3) The resolution authorising an off‑market purchase mentioned in
-- src:8547 | subsection (2) must state the particulars referred to in
-- src:8548 | subsection (2)(a), (b) and (c).
@ref s 76C(3) (src:8546-8548)
