      AND `the resolution states the maximum price which may be paid for the shares`
      AND `the resolution states the date on which the authority is to expire`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The resolution authorising an off-market purchase mentioned in subsection (2) must state the particulars referred to in subsection (2)(a), (b) and (c)" (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-C2} {MR-a}

-- src:8550 | (4) The authority for an off‑market purchase referred to in
-- src:8551 | subsection (2) may, from time to time, be varied or revoked by the
