-- src:8562 | discretion or opinion.
@ref s 76C(5) (src:8554-8562)
GIVEN `the resolution specifies a particular sum as the maximum price` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution provides a basis or formula for calculating the amount of the maximum price without reference to any person's discretion or opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76C(5) the resolution may determine the maximum price in this way` MEANS
    IF    `the resolution specifies a particular sum as the maximum price`
       OR `the resolution provides a basis or formula for calculating the amount of the maximum price without reference to any person's discretion or opinion`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may determine the maximum price for purchase or acquisition by — (a) specifying a particular sum; or (b) providing a basis or formula" lists two ways with no "only" {F-C4} {MR-b}

-- src:8564 | (6) For the purposes of this section and sections 76D and 76DA, an
-- src:8565 | “equal access scheme” means a scheme which satisfies all the
-- src:8566 | following conditions:
-- src:8568 | (a) the offers under the scheme are to be made to every person
-- src:8569 | who holds shares to purchase or acquire the same
-- src:8570 | percentage of their shares;
-- src:8572 | (b) all of those persons have a reasonable opportunity to accept
-- src:8573 | the offers made to them;
-- src:8575 | (c) the terms of all the offers are the same except that there
-- src:8576 | must be disregarded —
-- src:8578 | (i) differences in consideration attributable to the fact
-- src:8579 | that the offers relate to shares with different accrued
-- src:8580 | dividend entitlements;
-- src:8582 | (ii) differences in consideration attributable to the fact
-- src:8583 | that the offers relate to shares with different amounts
-- src:8584 | remaining unpaid; and
-- src:8586 | (iii) differences in the offers introduced solely to ensure
-- src:8587 | that each member is left with a whole number of
-- src:8588 | shares.
@ref s 76C(6) (src:8564-8588)
GIVEN `the offers under the scheme are to be made to every person who holds shares to purchase or acquire the same percentage of their shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all of those persons have a reasonable opportunity to accept the offers made to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms of all the offers are the same` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every difference between the terms of the offers is a difference in consideration attributable to shares with different accrued dividend entitlements, a difference in consideration attributable to shares with different amounts remaining unpaid, or a difference introduced solely to ensure that each member is left with a whole number of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76C(6) the scheme is an equal access scheme` MEANS
    IF    `the offers under the scheme are to be made to every person who holds shares to purchase or acquire the same percentage of their shares`
      AND `all of those persons have a reasonable opportunity to accept the offers made to them`
      AND (   `the terms of all the offers are the same`
           OR `every difference between the terms of the offers is a difference in consideration attributable to shares with different accrued dividend entitlements, a difference in consideration attributable to shares with different amounts remaining unpaid, or a difference introduced solely to ensure that each member is left with a whole number of shares`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an “equal access scheme” means a scheme which satisfies all the following conditions" (a "means" definition)

§ `Section 76D: authority for selective off-market acquisition`

-- src:8595 | 76D.—(1) A company may make a purchase or acquisition of its
-- src:8596 | own shares otherwise than on a securities exchange and not in
-- src:8597 | accordance with an equal access scheme (called in this section a
-- src:8598 | selective off‑market purchase) if the purchase or acquisition is made
-- src:8599 | in accordance with an agreement authorised in advance under
-- src:8600 | subsection (2).
@ref s 76D(1) (src:8595-8600)
GIVEN `the purchase or acquisition is made otherwise than on a securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with an equal access scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(1) the purchase or acquisition is a selective off-market purchase` MEANS
    IF    `the purchase or acquisition is made otherwise than on a securities exchange`
      AND (NOT `the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with an equal access scheme`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "otherwise than on a securities exchange and not in accordance with an equal access scheme (called in this section a selective off-market purchase)" (a definition) {MR-a}

-- src:8595 | 76D.—(1) A company may make a purchase or acquisition of its
-- src:8596 | own shares otherwise than on a securities exchange and not in
-- src:8597 | accordance with an equal access scheme (called in this section a
-- src:8598 | selective off‑market purchase) if the purchase or acquisition is made
-- src:8599 | in accordance with an agreement authorised in advance under
-- src:8600 | subsection (2).
@ref s 76D(1) (src:8595-8600)
GIVEN `the purchase or acquisition is a selective off-market purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with an agreement authorised in advance under section 76D(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(1) the company may make a selective off-market purchase or acquisition of its own shares` MEANS
    IF    `the purchase or acquisition is a selective off-market purchase`
      AND `the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with an agreement authorised in advance under section 76D(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("may make a purchase or acquisition of its own shares ... if the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with an agreement authorised in advance under subsection (2)") whose "if" gate failed; the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1 {F-D1} {MR-b}

-- (14) "associated person", in relation to a person: (a) the person's spouse, child or stepchild; or (b) a person who would, by virtue of section 7(5), be treated as an associate.
-- The keel's s 7(5) function is called for limb (b) (PLAN section 4, seam B).
-- src:8800 | (14) In this section, “associated person”, in relation to a person,
-- src:8801 | means —
-- src:8803 | (a) the person’s spouse, child or stepchild; or
-- src:8805 | (b) a person who would, by virtue of section 7(5), be treated as
-- src:8806 | an associate of the firstmentioned person.
@ref s 76D(14) (src:8800-8806)
GIVEN `the person is the spouse, child or stepchild of the firstmentioned person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a subsidiary of the firstmentioned person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is accustomed or under an obligation, formal or informal, to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the firstmentioned person in relation to the share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a body corporate that is, or a majority of the directors of which are, accustomed or under an obligation, formal or informal, to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the firstmentioned person in relation to the share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(14) the person is an associated person of the firstmentioned person` MEANS
    IF    `the person is the spouse, child or stepchild of the firstmentioned person`
       OR `s 7(5) the firstmentioned person is an associate of the other person` `the person is a subsidiary of the firstmentioned person` `the person is accustomed or under an obligation, formal or informal, to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the firstmentioned person in relation to the share` `the person is a body corporate that is, or a majority of the directors of which are, accustomed or under an obligation, formal or informal, to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the firstmentioned person in relation to the share` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“associated person”, in relation to a person, means — (a) ...; or (b) ..." (a "means" definition)

-- src:8604 | (2) The terms of the agreement for a selective off‑market purchase
-- src:8605 | must be authorised by a special resolution of the company, with no
-- src:8606 | votes being cast by any person whose shares are proposed to be
