-- src:8608 | subsections (3) to (13) apply with respect to that authority and to
-- src:8609 | resolutions conferring it.
@ref s 76D(2) (src:8604-8609)
GIVEN `the terms of the agreement have been authorised by a special resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a vote was cast on the resolution by a person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired, or by the person's associated persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(2) the terms of the agreement are authorised as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the terms of the agreement have been authorised by a special resolution of the company`
      AND (NOT `a vote was cast on the resolution by a person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired, or by the person's associated persons`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The terms of the agreement for a selective off-market purchase must be authorised by a special resolution of the company, with no votes being cast by any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired or by the person's associated persons" (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-D2} {MR-a}

-- The class consents added by Act 24 of 2025 (wef 06/05/2026): (2A) before the special resolution of (2); (5A) before the special resolution of (5); (9A) of (9); (12A) of (12).
-- "at least 75% of the holders": counted by holders, as the text says "holders" and not shares (fork F-D3).
-- src:8611 | (2A) Where the shares that are the subject of a selective off‑market
-- src:8612 | purchase mentioned in subsection (2) belong to a particular class of
-- src:8613 | shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class, the company
-- src:8614 | must, before passing the special resolution mentioned in that
-- src:8615 | subsection, obtain the consent of at least 75% of the holders of the
-- src:8616 | shares of that class (but excluding any person whose shares are
-- src:8617 | proposed to be purchased or acquired and the person’s associated
-- src:8618 | persons) to the terms of the agreement for the selective off-market
-- src:8619 | purchase.
@ref s 76D(2A) the threshold (src:8611-8619)
GIVEN `the number of holders of shares of the class whose consent is asked` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those holders who have consented` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 76D(2A) the consent of at least 75% of the holders has been obtained` MEANS
    (`the number of those holders who have consented` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (75 TIMES `the number of holders of shares of the class whose consent is asked`)

-- src:8611 | (2A) Where the shares that are the subject of a selective off‑market
-- src:8612 | purchase mentioned in subsection (2) belong to a particular class of
-- src:8613 | shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class, the company
-- src:8614 | must, before passing the special resolution mentioned in that
-- src:8615 | subsection, obtain the consent of at least 75% of the holders of the
-- src:8616 | shares of that class (but excluding any person whose shares are
-- src:8617 | proposed to be purchased or acquired and the person’s associated
-- src:8618 | persons) to the terms of the agreement for the selective off-market
-- src:8619 | purchase.
@ref s 76D(2A) (src:8611-8619)
GIVEN `the shares that are the subject of the selective off-market purchase belong to a particular class of shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of holders of shares of that class, excluding any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired and the person's associated persons` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those holders who have consented to the terms of the agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `the consent was obtained before the special resolution was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(2A) the company has obtained the consent the subsection requires before passing the special resolution` MEANS
    IF NOT `the shares that are the subject of the selective off-market purchase belong to a particular class of shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the shares ... belong to a particular class of shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class, the company must ... obtain the consent"; where that is not so the subsection requires no consent and says nothing of one (a duty whose "where" is unmet, decided site by site) {F-D4} {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF    `the consent was obtained before the special resolution was passed`
             AND `s 76D(2A) the consent of at least 75% of the holders has been obtained` `the number of holders of shares of that class, excluding any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired and the person's associated persons` `the number of those holders who have consented to the terms of the agreement`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must, before passing the special resolution mentioned in that subsection, obtain the consent of at least 75% of the holders of the shares of that class (but excluding any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired and the person's associated persons) to the terms of the agreement" (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-D3} {MR-a}

