          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired or any of the person's associated persons is not to be regarded as a member having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting of the company for the purposes of section 184A" (a flat negative) {MR-a}
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (a) says who is not regarded as a member with the right to vote; it does not say who is

-- src:8643 | (4A) If the special resolution mentioned in subsection (2) is
-- src:8644 | proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A —
-- src:8646 | (a) a person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or
-- src:8647 | acquired or any of the person’s associated persons is not to
-- src:8648 | be regarded as a member having the right to vote on the
-- src:8649 | resolution at a general meeting of the company for the
-- src:8650 | purposes of section 184A;
-- src:8652 | (b) subsection (7) does not apply; but all documents referred to
-- src:8653 | in this section must be given to all members having the
-- src:8654 | right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting for the
-- src:8655 | purposes of section 184A at or before the time —
-- src:8657 | (i) agreement to the resolution is sought in accordance
-- src:8658 | with section 184C; or
-- src:8660 | (ii) documents referred to in section 183(3A) in respect
-- src:8661 | of the resolution are served on or made accessible to
-- src:8662 | them in accordance with section 183(3A),
-- src:8664 | (b) as the case may be.
@ref s 76D(4A)(b) (src:8643-8664)
GIVEN `the special resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(4A)(b) section 76D(7) applies to the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the special resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (7) does not apply" (a flat negative) {MR-a}
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply" is said only of a resolution passed by written means under section 184A; for any other resolution subsection (7) is the rule in the ordinary way {MR-b}

-- src:8643 | (4A) If the special resolution mentioned in subsection (2) is
-- src:8644 | proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A —
-- src:8646 | (a) a person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or
-- src:8647 | acquired or any of the person’s associated persons is not to
-- src:8648 | be regarded as a member having the right to vote on the
-- src:8649 | resolution at a general meeting of the company for the
-- src:8650 | purposes of section 184A;
-- src:8652 | (b) subsection (7) does not apply; but all documents referred to
-- src:8653 | in this section must be given to all members having the
-- src:8654 | right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting for the
-- src:8655 | purposes of section 184A at or before the time —
-- src:8657 | (i) agreement to the resolution is sought in accordance
-- src:8658 | with section 184C; or
-- src:8660 | (ii) documents referred to in section 183(3A) in respect
-- src:8661 | of the resolution are served on or made accessible to
-- src:8662 | them in accordance with section 183(3A),
-- src:8664 | (b) as the case may be.
@ref s 76D(4A)(b) (src:8643-8664)
GIVEN `the special resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the documents referred to in section 76D were given to all members having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting at or before the time agreement to the resolution was sought in accordance with section 184C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the documents referred to in section 76D were served on or made accessible to all members having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting at or before the time the documents referred to in section 183(3A) were served on or made accessible to them in accordance with that section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(4A)(b) the documents have been given to the members in time` MEANS
    IF NOT `the special resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4A) begins "If the special resolution mentioned in subsection (2) is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A"; any other resolution is outside it {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF    `all the documents referred to in section 76D were given to all members having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting at or before the time agreement to the resolution was sought in accordance with section 184C`
             OR `all the documents referred to in section 76D were served on or made accessible to all members having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting at or before the time the documents referred to in section 183(3A) were served on or made accessible to them in accordance with that section`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all documents referred to in this section must be given to all members having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting for the purposes of section 184A at or before the time — (i) agreement to the resolution is sought ...; or (ii) documents referred to in section 183(3A) ... are served on or made accessible to them" (a duty not met, the provision's own question; the two limbs are taken as alternatives, "as the case may be") {F-D5} {MR-a}

-- src:8666 | (5) The authority referred to in subsection (2) may, from time to
-- src:8667 | time, be varied or revoked by a special resolution with no votes being
-- src:8668 | cast by any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or
-- src:8669 | acquired or by the person’s associated persons.
@ref s 76D(5) (src:8666-8669)
GIVEN `the authority is varied or revoked by a special resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a vote was cast on the resolution by a person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired, or by the person's associated persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(5) the authority for a selective off-market purchase may be varied or revoked` MEANS
    IF    `the authority is varied or revoked by a special resolution of the company`
      AND (NOT `a vote was cast on the resolution by a person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired, or by the person's associated persons`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("may, from time to time, be varied or revoked by a special resolution with no votes being cast by any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired or by the person's associated persons") whose named complement is absent {F-D6} {MR-b}

-- src:8671 | (5A) Where the shares that are the subject of the selective
-- src:8672 | off‑market purchase belong to a particular class of shares and do
-- src:8673 | not constitute all the shares in that class, the company must, before
-- src:8674 | passing the special resolution mentioned in subsection (5), obtain the
-- src:8675 | consent of at least 75% of the holders of the shares of that class (but
-- src:8676 | excluding any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or
-- src:8677 | acquired and the person’s associated persons) to the variation or
-- src:8678 | revocation of the authority (referred to in subsection (2)) mentioned
-- src:8679 | in subsection (5).
@ref s 76D(5A) (src:8671-8679)
GIVEN `the shares that are the subject of the selective off-market purchase belong to a particular class of shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of holders of shares of that class, excluding any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired and the person's associated persons` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those holders who have consented to the variation or revocation of the authority` IS A NUMBER
      `the consent was obtained before the special resolution was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(5A) the company has obtained the consent the subsection requires before passing the special resolution` MEANS
    IF NOT `the shares that are the subject of the selective off-market purchase belong to a particular class of shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the shares ... belong to a particular class of shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class, the company must ... obtain the consent"; where that is not so the subsection requires no consent and says nothing of one (a duty whose "where" is unmet, decided site by site) {F-D4} {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF    `the consent was obtained before the special resolution was passed`
             AND `s 76D(2A) the consent of at least 75% of the holders has been obtained` `the number of holders of shares of that class, excluding any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired and the person's associated persons` `the number of those holders who have consented to the variation or revocation of the authority`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must, before passing the special resolution mentioned in subsection (5), obtain the consent of at least 75% of the holders of the shares of that class (but excluding any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired and the person's associated persons) to the variation or revocation of the authority" (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-D3} {MR-a}

-- (6): how votes and poll demands are counted for (2) and (5).
-- src:8686 | (6) For the purposes of subsections (2) and (5) —
-- src:8688 | (a) a member or any of the member’s associated persons who
-- src:8689 | holds any of the shares to which the resolution relates is
-- src:8690 | regarded as exercising the voting rights carried by those
-- src:8691 | shares not only if the member or person votes in respect of
-- src:8692 | them on a poll on the question whether the resolution
-- src:8693 | should be passed, but also if the member or person votes on
-- src:8694 | the resolution otherwise than on a poll;
@ref s 76D(6)(a) (src:8686-8694)
GIVEN `the member or an associated person of the member holds shares to which the resolution relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member or person votes on the question on a poll` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member or person votes on the resolution otherwise than on a poll` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(6)(a) the member or person is regarded as exercising the voting rights carried by the shares` MEANS
    IF    `the member or an associated person of the member holds shares to which the resolution relates`
      AND (`the member or person votes on the question on a poll` OR `the member or person votes on the resolution otherwise than on a poll`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is regarded as exercising the voting rights ... not only if the member or person votes ... on a poll ..., but also if the member or person votes on the resolution otherwise than on a poll" extends the case and says nothing of a holder who does not vote {F-D7} {MR-b}

-- src:8686 | (6) For the purposes of subsections (2) and (5) —
-- src:8696 | (b) despite anything in the company’s constitution, any
-- src:8697 | member of the company may demand a poll on that
-- src:8698 | question; and
@ref s 76D(6)(b) (src:8686-8698)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(6)(b) the member may demand a poll on the question despite the company's constitution` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("any member of the company may demand a poll on that question"); a person who is not a member is outside it {F-D8} {MR-b}

-- src:8686 | (6) For the purposes of subsections (2) and (5) —
-- src:8700 | (c) a vote and a demand for a poll by a person as proxy for a
-- src:8701 | member or any of the member’s associated persons are the
-- src:8702 | same respectively as a vote and a demand by the member.
@ref s 76D(6)(c) (src:8686-8702)
GIVEN `the vote or demand is made by a person as proxy for a member or for any of the member's associated persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(6)(c) the vote or demand for a poll is the same as a vote or demand by the member` MEANS
    IF `the vote or demand is made by a person as proxy for a member or for any of the member's associated persons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a vote and a demand for a poll by a person as proxy for a member or any of the member's associated persons are the same respectively as a vote and a demand by the member"; a vote or demand not made by a proxy is outside it {MR-b}

-- (7): inspection. "not effective ... unless" -- JUST FALSE means not effective by this subsection's test. "15 days ending with the date of the meeting": the meeting day is the 15th day (fork F-P1).
-- src:8706 | (7) The special resolution mentioned in subsection (2) is not
-- src:8707 | effective for the purposes of this section unless (if the proposed
-- src:8708 | agreement is in writing) a copy of the agreement or (if not) a written
-- src:8709 | memorandum of its terms is available for inspection by members of
-- src:8710 | the company both —
-- src:8712 | (a) at the company’s registered office for not less than 15 days
-- src:8713 | ending with the date of the meeting at which the resolution
-- src:8714 | is passed; and
-- src:8716 | (b) at the meeting itself.
@ref s 76D(7)(a) (src:8706-8716)
GIVEN `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 76D(7)(a) the first day of the 15 days ending with the date of the meeting` MEANS
    `period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is passed` 14 Days

-- src:8706 | (7) The special resolution mentioned in subsection (2) is not
-- src:8707 | effective for the purposes of this section unless (if the proposed
-- src:8708 | agreement is in writing) a copy of the agreement or (if not) a written
-- src:8709 | memorandum of its terms is available for inspection by members of
-- src:8710 | the company both —
-- src:8712 | (a) at the company’s registered office for not less than 15 days
-- src:8713 | ending with the date of the meeting at which the resolution
-- src:8714 | is passed; and
-- src:8716 | (b) at the meeting itself.
@ref s 76D(7) (src:8706-8716)
GIVEN `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `the day from which the copy or memorandum has been continuously available for inspection by members at the company's registered office until the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the copy or memorandum is available for inspection by members at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(7) the special resolution is effective as far as the inspection requirement goes` MEANS
    IF    `the day from which the copy or memorandum has been continuously available for inspection by members at the company's registered office until the date of the meeting` AT MOST `s 76D(7)(a) the first day of the 15 days ending with the date of the meeting` `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is passed`
      AND `the copy or memorandum is available for inspection by members at the meeting itself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The special resolution mentioned in subsection (2) is not effective for the purposes of this section unless ... a copy of the agreement or ... a written memorandum of its terms is available for inspection by members of the company both — (a) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting ...; and (b) at the meeting itself" (an "unless" bar) {F-D9} {MR-a}

-- src:8718 | (8) A memorandum of terms so made available must include the
-- src:8719 | names of any members holding shares to which the agreement relates
-- src:8720 | and where a member holds such shares as nominee for another
-- src:8721 | person, the name of that other person; and a copy of the agreement so
-- src:8722 | made available must have annexed to it a written memorandum
-- src:8723 | specifying any such names which do not appear in the agreement
-- src:8724 | itself.
@ref s 76D(8) (src:8718-8724)
GIVEN `the agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum of terms includes the names of any members holding shares to which the agreement relates and, where a member holds such shares as nominee for another person, the name of that other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every such name appears in the agreement itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy of the agreement made available has annexed to it a written memorandum specifying any such names which do not appear in the agreement itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(8) the memorandum of terms or the copy of the agreement made available is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the agreement is in writing`
    THEN (IF    `every such name appears in the agreement itself`
             OR `the copy of the agreement made available has annexed to it a written memorandum specifying any such names which do not appear in the agreement itself`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a copy of the agreement so made available must have annexed to it a written memorandum specifying any such names which do not appear in the agreement itself" (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-D10} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF `the memorandum of terms includes the names of any members holding shares to which the agreement relates and, where a member holds such shares as nominee for another person, the name of that other person`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A memorandum of terms so made available must include the names of any members holding shares to which the agreement relates and where a member holds such shares as nominee for another person, the name of that other person" (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-D10} {MR-a}

-- src:8726 | (9) A company may agree to a variation of an existing agreement so
-- src:8727 | approved, but only if the variation is authorised, before it is agreed to,
-- src:8728 | by a special resolution of the company, with no votes being cast by
-- src:8733 | any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired or
-- src:8734 | by the person’s associated persons.
@ref s 76D(9) (src:8726-8734)
GIVEN `the variation is authorised, before it is agreed to, by a special resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a vote was cast on the resolution by a person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired, or by the person's associated persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(9) the company may agree to a variation of the existing agreement` MEANS
    IF    `the variation is authorised, before it is agreed to, by a special resolution of the company`
      AND (NOT `a vote was cast on the resolution by a person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired, or by the person's associated persons`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may agree to a variation of an existing agreement so approved, but only if the variation is authorised, before it is agreed to, by a special resolution of the company, with no votes being cast by any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired or by the person's associated persons" ("only if" closes the gate; the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 2) {F-D11} {MR-a}

-- src:8736 | (9A) Where the shares that are the subject of the selective
-- src:8737 | off‑market purchase belong to a particular class of shares and do
-- src:8738 | not constitute all the shares in that class, the company must, before
-- src:8739 | passing the special resolution mentioned in subsection (9), obtain the
-- src:8740 | consent of at least 75% of the holders of the shares of that class (but
-- src:8741 | excluding any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or
-- src:8742 | acquired and the person’s associated persons) to the variation of the
-- src:8743 | existing agreement mentioned in subsection (9).
@ref s 76D(9A) (src:8736-8743)
GIVEN `the shares that are the subject of the selective off-market purchase belong to a particular class of shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of holders of shares of that class, excluding any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired and the person's associated persons` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those holders who have consented to the variation of the existing agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `the consent was obtained before the special resolution was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(9A) the company has obtained the consent the subsection requires before passing the special resolution` MEANS
    IF NOT `the shares that are the subject of the selective off-market purchase belong to a particular class of shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the shares ... belong to a particular class of shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class, the company must ... obtain the consent"; where that is not so the subsection requires no consent and says nothing of one (a duty whose "where" is unmet, decided site by site) {F-D4} {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF    `the consent was obtained before the special resolution was passed`
             AND `s 76D(2A) the consent of at least 75% of the holders has been obtained` `the number of holders of shares of that class, excluding any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired and the person's associated persons` `the number of those holders who have consented to the variation of the existing agreement`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must, before passing the special resolution mentioned in subsection (9), obtain the consent of at least 75% of the holders of the shares of that class (but excluding any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired and the person's associated persons) to the variation of the existing agreement" (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-D3} {MR-a}

-- (10): subsections (3) to (7) apply to the authority for a proposed variation; the extra requirement is that the original agreement (or its memorandum) together with any variations previously made must also be available.
-- src:8747 | (10) Subsections (3) to (7) apply to the authority for a proposed
-- src:8748 | variation as they apply to the authority for a proposed agreement
-- src:8749 | except that a copy of the original agreement or (as the case may
-- src:8750 | require) a memorandum of its terms, together with any variations
-- src:8751 | previously made, must also be available for inspection in accordance
-- src:8752 | with subsection (7).
@ref s 76D(10) (src:8747-8752)
GIVEN `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `the day from which the copy or memorandum has been continuously available for inspection by members at the company's registered office until the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the copy or memorandum is available for inspection by members at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the original agreement or a memorandum of its terms, together with any variations previously made, is also available for inspection in accordance with subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(10) the special resolution for the variation is effective as far as the inspection requirement goes` MEANS
    IF    `s 76D(7) the special resolution is effective as far as the inspection requirement goes` `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is passed` `the day from which the copy or memorandum has been continuously available for inspection by members at the company's registered office until the date of the meeting` `the copy or memorandum is available for inspection by members at the meeting itself` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `a copy of the original agreement or a memorandum of its terms, together with any variations previously made, is also available for inspection in accordance with subsection (7)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (3) to (7) apply to the authority for a proposed variation as they apply to the authority for a proposed agreement except that a copy of the original agreement ... together with any variations previously made, must also be available for inspection in accordance with subsection (7)" (subsection (7)'s "unless" carried over to the variation) {F-D9} {MR-a}

-- src:8754 | (11) The rights of a company under an agreement for a selective
-- src:8755 | off‑market purchase approved under this section are not capable of
-- src:8756 | being assigned except by order of the Court made pursuant to any
-- src:8757 | provision of this Act or any other written law.
@ref s 76D(11) (src:8754-8757)
GIVEN `the Court has made an order, under a provision of this Act or of any other written law, that the rights be assigned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(11) the rights of the company under the approved agreement are barred from being assigned` MEANS
    IF `the Court has made an order, under a provision of this Act or of any other written law, that the rights be assigned`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are not capable of being assigned except by order of the Court made pursuant to any provision of this Act or any other written law" -- the "except" is met, so the bar is gone (an "except" once met, decided site by site) {F-D12} {MR-a}
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:8759 | (12) An agreement by a company to release its rights under an
-- src:8760 | agreement for a selective off‑market purchase approved under this
-- src:8761 | section is void unless the terms of the release agreement are approved
-- src:8762 | in advance before the agreement is entered into by a special resolution
-- src:8763 | of the company with no votes being cast by any person whose shares
-- src:8764 | are proposed to be purchased or acquired or by the person’s
-- src:8765 | associated persons; and subsections (3) to (7) apply to the approval
-- src:8766 | for a proposed release agreement as they apply to authority for the
-- src:8767 | proposed variation of an existing agreement.
@ref s 76D(12) (src:8759-8767)
GIVEN `the terms of the release agreement are approved in advance, before the agreement is entered into, by a special resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a vote was cast on the resolution by a person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired, or by the person's associated persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(12) the agreement by the company to release its rights is void` MEANS
    IF    `the terms of the release agreement are approved in advance, before the agreement is entered into, by a special resolution of the company`
      AND (NOT `a vote was cast on the resolution by a person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired, or by the person's associated persons`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is void unless the terms of the release agreement are approved in advance ... by a special resolution of the company with no votes being cast by any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired or by the person's associated persons" -- the "unless" is met, so subsection (12) does not make it void {F-D12} {MR-a}
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:8769 | (12A) Where the shares that are the subject of the selective
-- src:8770 | off‑market purchase belong to a particular class of shares and do not
-- src:8771 | constitute all the shares in that class, the company must, before
-- src:8772 | passing the special resolution mentioned in subsection (12), obtain
-- src:8773 | the consent of at least 75% of the holders of the shares of that class to
-- src:8778 | the terms of the proposed release agreement mentioned in subsection
-- src:8779 | (12).
@ref s 76D(12A) (src:8769-8779)
GIVEN `the shares that are the subject of the selective off-market purchase belong to a particular class of shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of holders of shares of that class` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those holders who have consented to the terms of the proposed release agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `the consent was obtained before the special resolution was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(12A) the company has obtained the consent the subsection requires before passing the special resolution` MEANS
    IF NOT `the shares that are the subject of the selective off-market purchase belong to a particular class of shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the shares ... belong to a particular class of shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class, the company must ... obtain the consent"; where that is not so the subsection requires no consent and says nothing of one (a duty whose "where" is unmet, decided site by site) {F-D4} {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF    `the consent was obtained before the special resolution was passed`
             AND `s 76D(2A) the consent of at least 75% of the holders has been obtained` `the number of holders of shares of that class` `the number of those holders who have consented to the terms of the proposed release agreement`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must, before passing the special resolution mentioned in subsection (12), obtain the consent of at least 75% of the holders of the shares of that class to the terms of the proposed release agreement" (a duty not met, the provision's own question; unlike (2A), (5A) and (9A) the text does not exclude the sellers and their associated persons here, fork F-D3) {F-D3} {MR-a}

-- src:8783 | (12B) To avoid doubt, the consent mentioned in subsection (2A),
-- src:8784 | (5A), (9A) or (12A) includes, but is not limited to, consent given by a
-- src:8785 | resolution passed at a meeting of the holders mentioned in that
-- src:8786 | subsection.
@ref s 76D(12B) (src:8783-8786)
GIVEN `the consent is given by a resolution passed at a meeting of the holders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(12B) the consent is within the consent mentioned in subsection (2A), (5A), (9A) or (12A)` MEANS
    IF `the consent is given by a resolution passed at a meeting of the holders`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes, but is not limited to, consent given by a resolution passed at a meeting of the holders"; other forms of consent are not excluded and not listed

-- src:8790 | (13) A resolution to confer or vary authority for a selective
-- src:8791 | off‑market purchase under this section may determine the
-- src:8792 | maximum price for purchase or acquisition by —
-- src:8794 | (a) specifying a particular sum; or
-- src:8796 | (b) providing a basis or formula for calculating the amount of
-- src:8797 | the price in question without reference to any person’s
-- src:8798 | discretion or opinion.
@ref s 76D(13) (src:8790-8798)
GIVEN `the resolution specifies a particular sum as the maximum price` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution provides a basis or formula for calculating the amount of the maximum price without reference to any person's discretion or opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76D(13) the resolution may determine the maximum price in this way` MEANS
    IF    `the resolution specifies a particular sum as the maximum price`
       OR `the resolution provides a basis or formula for calculating the amount of the maximum price without reference to any person's discretion or opinion`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may determine the maximum price for purchase or acquisition by — (a) specifying a particular sum; or (b) providing a basis or formula" lists two ways with no "only" {F-C4} {MR-b}

§ `Section 76DA: contingent purchase contract`

-- src:8810 | 76DA.—(1) A company may, whether or not it is listed on an
-- src:8811 | approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside
-- src:8812 | Singapore, make a purchase or acquisition of its own shares under a
-- src:8813 | contingent purchase contract if the proposed contingent purchase
-- src:8814 | contract is authorised in advance by a special resolution of the
-- src:8815 | company.
@ref s 76DA(1) (src:8810-8815)
GIVEN `the proposed contingent purchase contract is authorised in advance by a special resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76DA(1) the company may make a purchase or acquisition of its own shares under a contingent purchase contract` MEANS
    IF `the proposed contingent purchase contract is authorised in advance by a special resolution of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("A company may, whether or not it is listed ..., make a purchase or acquisition of its own shares under a contingent purchase contract if the proposed contingent purchase contract is authorised in advance by a special resolution of the company") whose "if" gate failed; the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1 {F-DA1} {MR-b}

-- src:8819 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), the authority under subsection (1)
-- src:8820 | may, from time to time, be varied or revoked by a special resolution of
-- src:8821 | the company.
@ref s 76DA(2) (src:8819-8821)
GIVEN `the authority is varied or revoked by a special resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76DA(2) the authority for a contingent purchase contract may be varied or revoked` MEANS
    IF `the authority is varied or revoked by a special resolution of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("may, from time to time, be varied or revoked by a special resolution of the company") whose named complement is absent {F-DA1} {MR-b}

-- src:8823 | (3) The notice specifying the intention to propose a special
-- src:8824 | resolution to authorise a contingent purchase contract must specify
-- src:8825 | a date on which the authority is to expire and that date must not be
-- src:8830 | later than the date on which the next annual general meeting of the
-- src:8831 | company is or is required by law to be held, whichever is the earlier.
@ref s 76DA(3) (src:8823-8831)
GIVEN `the date specified in the notice on which the authority is to expire` IS A DATE
      `the date the next annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE
      `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76DA(3) the notice specifying the intention to propose the special resolution has the content the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `s 76C(2)(c) the expiry date is not later than the date of the next annual general meeting` `the date specified in the notice on which the authority is to expire` `the date the next annual general meeting is held` `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice specifying the intention to propose a special resolution to authorise a contingent purchase contract must specify a date on which the authority is to expire and that date must not be later than the date on which the next annual general meeting of the company is or is required by law to be held, whichever is the earlier" (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-DA2} {MR-a}

-- This period is counted with the day named as day 1, so the keel is called with the count less one (fork F-P1).
-- src:8833 | (4) The special resolution mentioned in subsection (1) is invalid for
-- src:8834 | the purposes of this section unless a copy of the proposed contingent
-- src:8835 | purchase contract is available for inspection by members of the
-- src:8836 | company —
-- src:8838 | (a) at the company’s registered office for not less than 15 days
-- src:8839 | ending with the date of the meeting at which the resolution
-- src:8840 | is passed; and
-- src:8842 | (b) at the meeting itself.
@ref s 76DA(4) (src:8833-8842)
GIVEN `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `the day from which a copy of the proposed contingent purchase contract has been continuously available for inspection by members at the company's registered office until the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `a copy of the proposed contingent purchase contract is available for inspection by members at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76DA(4) the special resolution is valid as far as the inspection requirement goes` MEANS
    IF    `the day from which a copy of the proposed contingent purchase contract has been continuously available for inspection by members at the company's registered office until the date of the meeting` AT MOST `s 76D(7)(a) the first day of the 15 days ending with the date of the meeting` `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is passed`
      AND `a copy of the proposed contingent purchase contract is available for inspection by members at the meeting itself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The special resolution mentioned in subsection (1) is invalid for the purposes of this section unless a copy of the proposed contingent purchase contract is available for inspection by members of the company — (a) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting at which the resolution is passed; and (b) at the meeting itself" (an "unless" bar) {F-DA3} {MR-a}

-- src:8844 | (5) A company may agree to a variation of an existing contingent
-- src:8845 | purchase contract so approved if, and only if, the variation is
-- src:8846 | authorised, before it is agreed to, by a special resolution of the
-- src:8847 | company.
@ref s 76DA(5) (src:8844-8847)
GIVEN `the variation is authorised, before it is agreed to, by a special resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76DA(5) the company may agree to a variation of the existing contingent purchase contract` MEANS
    IF `the variation is authorised, before it is agreed to, by a special resolution of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may agree to a variation of an existing contingent purchase contract so approved if, and only if, the variation is authorised, before it is agreed to, by a special resolution of the company" ("if, and only if" closes the gate; the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 2) {F-DA4} {MR-a}

-- src:8849 | (6) Subsections (2), (3) and (4) apply to the authority for a proposed
-- src:8850 | variation as they apply to the authority for a proposed contingent
-- src:8851 | purchase contract, except that a copy of the original contract, together
-- src:8852 | with any variations previously made, must also be available for
-- src:8853 | inspection in accordance with subsection (4).
@ref s 76DA(6) (src:8849-8853)
GIVEN `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `the day from which a copy of the proposed contingent purchase contract has been continuously available for inspection by members at the company's registered office until the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `a copy of the proposed contingent purchase contract is available for inspection by members at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the original contract, together with any variations previously made, is also available for inspection in accordance with subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76DA(6) the special resolution for the variation is valid as far as the inspection requirement goes` MEANS
    IF    `s 76DA(4) the special resolution is valid as far as the inspection requirement goes` `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is passed` `the day from which a copy of the proposed contingent purchase contract has been continuously available for inspection by members at the company's registered office until the date of the meeting` `a copy of the proposed contingent purchase contract is available for inspection by members at the meeting itself` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `a copy of the original contract, together with any variations previously made, is also available for inspection in accordance with subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (2), (3) and (4) apply to the authority for a proposed variation as they apply to the authority for a proposed contingent purchase contract, except that a copy of the original contract, together with any variations previously made, must also be available for inspection in accordance with subsection (4)" (subsection (4)'s "unless" carried over to the variation) {F-DA3} {MR-a}

-- src:8855 | (7) The company may only make an offer to enter into a contingent
-- src:8856 | purchase contract in accordance with all of the following conditions:
-- src:8858 | (a) the offer must be made to every person who holds shares of
-- src:8859 | the same class in the company;
-- src:8861 | (b) the number of shares that a company is obliged or entitled
-- src:8862 | to purchase or acquire under the contract from any person,
-- src:8863 | in relation to the total number of shares of the same class
-- src:8864 | held by that person, must be of the same proportion for
-- src:8865 | every person who holds shares of that class to whom the
-- src:8866 | offer is made;
-- src:8868 | (c) the terms of all offers in respect of each class of shares
-- src:8869 | must be the same.
@ref s 76DA(7) (src:8855-8869)
GIVEN `the offer is made to every person who holds shares of the same class in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of shares that the company is obliged or entitled to purchase or acquire under the contract from any person, in relation to the total number of shares of the same class held by that person, is of the same proportion for every person who holds shares of that class to whom the offer is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms of all offers in respect of each class of shares are the same` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76DA(7) the company may make the offer to enter into a contingent purchase contract` MEANS
    IF    `the offer is made to every person who holds shares of the same class in the company`
      AND `the number of shares that the company is obliged or entitled to purchase or acquire under the contract from any person, in relation to the total number of shares of the same class held by that person, is of the same proportion for every person who holds shares of that class to whom the offer is made`
      AND `the terms of all offers in respect of each class of shares are the same`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company may only make an offer to enter into a contingent purchase contract in accordance with all of the following conditions" ("only" closes the list; the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 2) {F-DA4} {MR-a}

-- src:8871 | (8) To avoid doubt, the company may purchase or acquire shares
-- src:8872 | under a contingent purchase contract from any person whether or not
-- src:8873 | the offer to enter into the contract was originally made to the person.
@ref s 76DA(8) (src:8871-8873)
GIVEN `the person is a person from whom the company proposes to purchase or acquire shares under the contingent purchase contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer to enter into the contract was originally made to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76DA(8) the company may purchase or acquire shares under the contingent purchase contract from the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a person from whom the company proposes to purchase or acquire shares under the contingent purchase contract`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the answer does not depend on whether the offer was originally made to the person: "whether or not the offer to enter into the contract was originally made to the person"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says the company may purchase from "any person" under the contract; a case with no purchase from a person under the contract is outside it

-- src:8878 | (9) In this section, “contingent purchase contract” means a contract
-- src:8879 | entered into by a company and relating to any of its shares —
-- src:8881 | (a) which does not amount to a contract to purchase or acquire
-- src:8882 | those shares; but
-- src:8884 | (b) under which the company may (subject to any condition)
-- src:8885 | become entitled or obliged to purchase or acquire those
-- src:8886 | shares.
@ref s 76DA(9) (src:8878-8886)
GIVEN `the contract was entered into by a company and relates to any of its shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract does not amount to a contract to purchase or acquire those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the contract the company may (subject to any condition) become entitled or obliged to purchase or acquire those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76DA(9) the contract is a contingent purchase contract` MEANS
    IF    `the contract was entered into by a company and relates to any of its shares`
      AND `the contract does not amount to a contract to purchase or acquire those shares`
      AND `under the contract the company may (subject to any condition) become entitled or obliged to purchase or acquire those shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“contingent purchase contract” means a contract entered into by a company and relating to any of its shares — (a) which does not amount to a contract to purchase or acquire those shares; but (b) under which the company may (subject to any condition) become entitled or obliged to purchase or acquire those shares" (a "means" definition)

§ `Section 76E: authority for market acquisition`

-- (1): a bar. TRUE: a market purchase made without advance authority. FALSE: the authority was given. NOTHING: not a purchase on a securities exchange.
-- src:8890 | 76E.—(1) A company must not make a purchase or acquisition of
-- src:8891 | its own shares on a securities exchange (called in this section a market
-- src:8892 | purchase) unless the purchase or acquisition has been authorised in
-- src:8893 | advance by the company in general meeting.
@ref s 76E(1) (src:8890-8893)
GIVEN `the purchase or acquisition is made on a securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase or acquisition has been authorised in advance by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76E(1) the company is barred from making the market purchase` MEANS
    IF NOT `the purchase or acquisition is made on a securities exchange`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is of a purchase "on a securities exchange (called in this section a market purchase)"; a purchase elsewhere is outside it {F-E1} {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF `the purchase or acquisition has been authorised in advance by the company in general meeting`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must not make a purchase or acquisition of its own shares on a securities exchange ... unless the purchase or acquisition has been authorised in advance by the company in general meeting" -- the "unless" is met {F-E1} {MR-a}
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:8895 | (2) The notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution to
-- src:8896 | authorise a market purchase must —
-- src:8898 | (a) specify the maximum number of shares or the maximum
-- src:8899 | percentage of ordinary shares authorised to be purchased
-- src:8900 | or acquired;
-- src:8902 | (b) determine the maximum price which may be paid for the
-- src:8903 | shares;
-- src:8905 | (c) specify a date on which the authority is to expire, being a
-- src:8906 | date that must not be later than the date on which the next
-- src:8907 | annual general meeting of the company is or is required by
-- src:8908 | law to be held, whichever is the earlier; and
-- src:8910 | (d) specify the sources of funds to be used for the purchase or
-- src:8911 | acquisition including the amount of financing and its
-- src:8912 | impact on the company’s financial position.
@ref s 76E(2) (src:8895-8912)
GIVEN `the notice specifies the maximum number of shares or the maximum percentage of ordinary shares authorised to be purchased or acquired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice determines the maximum price which may be paid for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date specified in the notice on which the authority is to expire` IS A DATE
      `the date the next annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE
      `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held` IS A DATE
      `the notice specifies the sources of funds to be used for the purchase or acquisition including the amount of financing and its impact on the company's financial position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76E(2) the notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution has the content the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the notice specifies the maximum number of shares or the maximum percentage of ordinary shares authorised to be purchased or acquired`
      AND `the notice determines the maximum price which may be paid for the shares`
      AND `s 76C(2)(c) the expiry date is not later than the date of the next annual general meeting` `the date specified in the notice on which the authority is to expire` `the date the next annual general meeting is held` `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held`
      AND `the notice specifies the sources of funds to be used for the purchase or acquisition including the amount of financing and its impact on the company's financial position`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution to authorise a market purchase must — (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; and (d) ..." (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-E2} {MR-a}

-- src:8916 | (3) The authority for a market purchase may be unconditional or
-- src:8917 | subject to conditions and must state the particulars referred to in
-- src:8918 | subsection (2)(a), (b) and (c).
@ref s 76E(3) (src:8916-8918)
GIVEN `the authority states the maximum number of shares or the maximum percentage of ordinary shares authorised to be purchased or acquired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority states the maximum price which may be paid for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority states the date on which it is to expire` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76E(3) the authority for a market purchase states the particulars the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the authority states the maximum number of shares or the maximum percentage of ordinary shares authorised to be purchased or acquired`
      AND `the authority states the maximum price which may be paid for the shares`
      AND `the authority states the date on which it is to expire`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The authority for a market purchase may be unconditional or subject to conditions and must state the particulars referred to in subsection (2)(a), (b) and (c)" (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-E2} {MR-a}

-- src:8920 | (4) The authority for a market purchase may, from time to time, be
-- src:8921 | varied or revoked by the company in general meeting but the
-- src:8922 | variation must comply with subsections (2) and (3).
@ref s 76E(4) (src:8920-8922)
GIVEN `the authority is varied or revoked by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change to the authority is a variation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the variation complies with subsections (2) and (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76E(4) the authority for a market purchase may be varied or revoked` MEANS
    IF    `the authority is varied or revoked by the company in general meeting`
      AND ((NOT `the change to the authority is a variation`) OR `the variation complies with subsections (2) and (3)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("may, from time to time, be varied or revoked by the company in general meeting but the variation must comply with subsections (2) and (3)") whose named complement or condition is absent {F-E3} {MR-b}

-- src:8927 | (5) A resolution to confer or vary authority for a market purchase
-- src:8928 | under this section may determine the maximum price for purchase or
-- src:8929 | acquisition by —
-- src:8931 | (a) specifying a particular sum; or
-- src:8933 | (b) providing a basis or formula for calculating the amount of
-- src:8934 | the price in question without reference to any person’s
-- src:8935 | discretion or opinion.
@ref s 76E(5) (src:8927-8935)
GIVEN `the resolution specifies a particular sum as the maximum price` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution provides a basis or formula for calculating the amount of the maximum price without reference to any person's discretion or opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76E(5) the resolution may determine the maximum price in this way` MEANS
    IF    `the resolution specifies a particular sum as the maximum price`
       OR `the resolution provides a basis or formula for calculating the amount of the maximum price without reference to any person's discretion or opinion`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may determine the maximum price for purchase or acquisition by — (a) specifying a particular sum; or (b) providing a basis or formula" lists two ways with no "only" {F-C4} {MR-b}

§ `Regulative rule: s 76E(1), the prohibition derived from the bar`

DECLARE `s 76E act` IS ONE OF
    `s 76E(1) make a purchase or acquisition of its own shares on a securities exchange without authority given in advance by the company in general meeting`

-- The text names the bearer (the company) and the act, so the prohibition is derived (ruling N2 of 2026-11-04). With the authority given, nothing is owed and the rule reads FULFILLED.
-- src:8890 | 76E.—(1) A company must not make a purchase or acquisition of
-- src:8891 | its own shares on a securities exchange (called in this section a market
-- src:8892 | purchase) unless the purchase or acquisition has been authorised in
-- src:8893 | advance by the company in general meeting.
@ref s 76E(1) (src:8890-8893)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the purchase or acquisition has been authorised in advance by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 76E act`
`s 76E(1) the company must not make a market purchase unless it is authorised in advance` MEANS
    IF `the purchase or acquisition has been authorised in advance by the company in general meeting`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY Company `the name of the company`
         SHANT `s 76E(1) make a purchase or acquisition of its own shares on a securities exchange without authority given in advance by the company in general meeting`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company made a market purchase of its own shares that had not been authorised in advance by the company in general meeting"
